 "narrative": {
  "northStar": "One white sheet on a quiet desk",
  "overview": "The product is a light, airy, premium SaaS tool. The user chose it on 2026-10-26, with Halo Lab's \"Bubdle\" as the reference, after rejecting the photocopy, guide-map, blue-pencil, red-claim-form and colour-chapter worlds. The anti-slop rules of taste-skill v2 take priority over the reference. A flat grey ground (#EDEDEC) holds the sidebar and the context line. All the work sits on one white sheet with 28px corners, and every group on that sheet is a soft grey card, one tone step away. Nothing is outlined, nothing casts a resting shadow and nothing uses a gradient. Type is Switzer, set large and light: titles at 400 weight with tight tracking, the verdict at 28px (ink, with only its glyph in the status hue), the days-left figure at 36px, and body text at 14px.\n\nThe density suits a biller working a queue: 64px worklist rows, a 372px rules ledger beside the policy text, and a 320px citation gate beside the appeal letter. Colour is kept for meaning. Green, amber and red mark evidence and verdict status, and always come with a glyph and a word. Blue (#1E4BD7) means only \"verified against text fetched for this case\" (and the focus ring). Everything else is ink on grey and white.\n\nThe signature is the verified disc: a filled blue circle with a white check. It marks each quote in the letter and each line in the citation gate. As the gate confirms, the checks draw in from top to bottom, which is the one authored motion in the product. A tampered quote is struck through in red and marked \"Not in source\" with a cross glyph, and the source's real words appear beneath it.",
  "keyCharacteristics": [
   "Flat grey frame (#EDEDEC) around one white sheet (28px corners). From tablet up the sheet is as tall as its page, so a short list ends with its own content on the grey ground rather than holding an empty band; on a phone the sheet runs edge to edge with 22px top corners down to the bottom bar.",
   "Cards are #F5F5F4 on the white sheet, separated by tone alone, with no outline and no shadow.",
   "Pill controls: black primary buttons, grey secondary buttons, pill inputs, pill filters and pill status marks.",
   "Switzer only (self-hosted, weights 400, 500 and 600), on a six-step scale: 12, 14, 16, 18, 28 and 36px.",
   "Status = hue + glyph + word. Blue = verified, and nothing else."
  ],
  "rules": [
   {
    "name": "The One Blue Rule",
